  "question": {
    "text": "Two charges, each equal to $-q$ are kept at $(-a, 0)$ and $(a, 0)$. A charge $q$ is placed at the origin. If $q$ is given a small displacement along y direction, the force acting on q is proportional to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YZ0Fi",
      "text": "$y$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "crOHF",
      "text": "-y",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "W9Ure",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{y}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FTmwF",
      "text": "$-\\frac{1}{y}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/t7TQ3LqJc-JSEbuvMknpZS5icu7vTFH6H9NU7ErQnIo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\vec{F}=+q$ (Electric field due to the two negative charges $=\\vec{E}$ )\n$$\n\\vec{F}=+q\\left[\\frac{k(-2 q) \\vec{y}}{a^3}\\right] \\Rightarrow \\vec{F}=-\\frac{2 k q^2 y}{a^3} \\Rightarrow \\vec{F} \\propto-\\vec{y}\n$$",
    "image": null
